Spec: TenantDeleteScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Orchestrate the teardown of one `TenantInstance`: run the package's category buckets in the
  reverse of the install build-up through @import_run — `delete_pre` hook, `posts`, `scalables`,
  tofu destroy, `others`, backup sweep plus `vitals`, `befores` — then the `delete_post` hook,
  and return. This file applies no deletes itself and writes nothing: the per-bucket cluster
  deletions walk the `instance.status` lists that install recorded, inside the stage modules it
  dispatches; and it is not the close-out either — zero `status` write, zero condition, zero
  finalizer or CR removal here and in the shipped tenant delete stages. A clean return only
  carries the delete Job out of Rust happy-path (agent exit `0`) so the controller's
  @do_cleanup sees a `Complete` job, answers @Action::await_change() and the
  @run_with_finalizer wrapper releases the `tenantinstances.vynil.solidite.fr` finalizer
  (/operator/src/instance_common.sdd).
  Twin: near-clone of ./../service/delete.rhai — an actual `diff -u` shows exactly ONE hunk:
  the tenant copy drops the whole `crds` bucket block (its `@is_dir` gate,
  `@import_run("delete_crds")` and map merge) between the `befores` lane and the `delete_post`
  hook and is byte-identical otherwise, call names verbatim. The absence is sound: the tenant
  CRD family carries no CRD-stage surface at all — no `CrdApplied` condition, no crd bridge, and
  @TenantInstanceStatus has no `crds` key (/common/src/instancetenant.sdd). Six of this lane's
  seven stage modules are likewise byte-identical copies of the service ones; only
  ./delete_vitals.rhai differs, by a commented-out final-backup block (Tasks).
  ./../system/delete.rhai is the different shape (single `systems` bucket, no vitals/backup
  section).

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @context) — the module's sole @fn and entry point (`delete.rhai` + `run`
    match the entry-point patterns of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd); invoked as
    `delete::run(instance, context)` by the Rust lane /agent/src/tenant/delete.sdd, whose
    snippet discards the returned value.

Accepts:
  @instance — the injected @TenantInstance @Dynamic, the one CR the Rust lane fetched before the
    script. Never read and never re-bound: this file touches zero properties of it (no `.status`
    read, no @get_tenant_instance refresh — ./install.rhai's six per-bucket refreshes have no
    delete-side counterpart); it only relays it as the first argument to all nine @import_run
    calls. The `instance.status.<category>` reads the stages perform see exactly the pre-script
    CR snapshot.
  @context — map built by ./context.rhai @run for this lane (core keys from
    ./../lib/build_context.rhai merged with the tenant additions of ./context_tenant.rhai; key
    contracts in ./context.sdd, ./context_tenant.sdd), unless a `context.rhai` under an earlier
    resolver directory shadows it. Only key read here: `package_dir` (unguarded property access
    feeding the six gate interpolations — five @is_dir paths and the one @has_tofu_files path);
    every other key is consumed by the stage modules, which receive the whole maps.

Returns:
  No value channel of its own: the function's implicit value is the trailing
    `@import_run("delete_post", ...)` result (`()` on a stock image, the hook ships nowhere) and
    the caller discards it. No observable artifact of its own — no `status` patch, no event, no
    finalizer touch, no CR deletion. Success is observable as the cluster objects the stages
    deleted plus the exit-`0`/exit-`3` outcome the clean-return-or-raise produces; the delete's
    completion itself belongs to the operator's finalizer release quoted in `Purpose`.

Raises:
  Zero @throw statement in this file: failure is always a propagated engine raise landing in
    the Rust exit(`3`) lane (/agent/src/tenant/mod.sdd text `Deleting a package failed with:`).
  - Stage/hook module throw: @import_run swallows only the absent-module and absent-`run`
    markers (`log_debug` with text `No ${name} module, skipping.` /
    `No ${name}::run function, skipping.`, vynil-core shim semantics); any other error
    re-throws and aborts. Unlike the install lanes (their `set_status_*_failed` markers), the
    shipped tenant delete stages carry no `set_status_` call at all — none in any `delete_*.rhai`
    of this directory — so a stage raise leaves no delete-side failure marker on the CR; the
    error text is all the record (retry posture owned by the operator).
  - @has_tofu_files raise: the tofu gate runs its predicate over an unreadable existing
    `${package_dir}/tofu` past the module-internal @is_dir guard (rules in ./../lib/tofu_gen.sdd).
  - Import-time raise: an unresolvable `tofu_gen` module (or its transitive `tofu`) fails the
    module load before @run ever starts; the Rust lane resolves `delete` lazily, after any
    `ctx::run` side effects (/agent/src/tenant/delete.sdd).
  - Property-on-`()` raise after the tofu lane: that lane assigns `context = @import_run(...)`
    unguarded, so a resolved `delete_tofu` whose `run` is missing or returns a non-map leaves
    `context` = `()` and the very next gate `${context.package_dir}/others` raises mid-file
    with a non-stage error (Tasks).

Handles:
  - Bucket-directory absent: the @is_dir gate (`@has_tofu_files` for tofu) skips the whole
    lane — including the teardown of status-recorded entries for that category (status-versus-dir
    orphan point in Tasks). A missing lane module does not raise; it takes the @import_run
    skip path.
  - Bucket-directory present but nothing installed (`status` missing, or no key for the
    category — e.g. delete of an imported-but-never-installed CR): the lane still runs; each
    shipped bucket stage guards the set-ness of `instance.status` and of
    `instance.status.<category>` (both must not be `()`) and degrades to hook-noop while
    returning the context — a dir-full, never-installed package runs every lane and mutates
    nothing.
  - `delete_pre` / `delete_post` ship nowhere under ./agent/scripts — on a stock image both
    hooks take the @import_run skip path, return `()`, and the `type_of` merge guard sees no
    map (the hook pair exists only as package-side scripts under {package_dir}/scripts).
  - Package carrying a `crds/` directory: ignored entirely by this lane — there is no crd
    bucket and no tenant-side `delete_crds` module to import; the tenant kind records no crd
    state, so package-CR cleanup needs another actor (see Purpose).
  - Backup sweep rides the `vitals` gate: `@import_run("delete_backup")` executes before
    `@import_run("delete_vitals")` only when `${package_dir}/vitals` is a directory, and its
    return — including any `delete_backup_prepare` hook context the module merged — is
    discarded whole (a package that never carried `vitals/` never sweeps its backup objects on
    delete, even though tenant INSTALL sweeps `delete_backup` on every run per ./install.sdd —
    Tasks).
  - Context threading: @type_of == `map` merge only — `delete_pre` and the five `is_dir`
    buckets use the guard; the shipped bucket stages always return a context map (identity
    merge unless their own `delete_<category>_pre` / `..._post` inner hooks merged, pending
    specs); the `delete_tofu` lane is the unguarded assignment; `delete_backup` and
    `delete_post` returns are discarded.

Must:
  Run exactly these lanes, once each, in this order: `@import_run("delete_pre")` with the map
    merge; `@is_dir(`${context.package_dir}/posts`)` gate → `@import_run("delete_posts", ...)`;
    `scalables` gate → `delete_scalables`;
    `@tfg::has_tofu_files(`${context.package_dir}/tofu`)` gate →
    `context = @import_run("delete_tofu", instance, context)` — the single guard-free assign;
    `others` gate → `delete_others`; `vitals` gate → `@import_run("delete_backup", ...)` first,
    then `delete_vitals`; `befores` gate → `delete_befores`;
    `@import_run("delete_post", instance, context)` with no merge and no read of the result —
    then return, nothing after the hook. No `crds` lane anywhere in this sequence.
  Keep the order the `./install.rhai` bucket order reversed (install is `befores → vitals →
    tofu → others → scalables → posts` per ./install.sdd; delete is `posts → scalables → … →
    others → vitals → befores`), with one deliberate deviation: the tofu lane sits third, BEFORE
    `others`, not mirrored fourth (verbatim order above, not a pure mirror claim) — the same
    deviation its service twin ships.
  Rebuild every gate predicate from the CURRENT `context` at evaluation time: a hook or stage
    that merged a map may change `package_dir`, and earlier skip decisions are never revisited.
  Relay @instance unchanged and unread to every lane: no @get_tenant_instance refresh exists
    at this level, so all nine lanes observe the one `status` snapshot from the pre-script Rust
    fetch — the asymmetry with ./install.rhai is exact (install refreshed because its buckets
    wrote `status`; delete stages write none).
  Emit no log at this level: no @log_info/@log_warn/@log_debug statement (./install.rhai's two
    probe-catch warnings have no delete counterpart); all delete observability sits in the
    stage modules and the shim's skip debugs.
  Load ./../lib/tofu_gen.rhai (and transitively ./../lib/tofu.rhai) at import time via the
    single top-level `import "tofu_gen" as tfg` — before any `run` call, packages without any
    `.tf` file included; it is the only import-time statement besides the @fn declaration.
  Resolve every stage/hook module against the four resolver directories frozen by the Rust lane
    (`{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}`, `{script_dir}/tenant`, `{script_dir}/lib`, earlier
    wins), so a package `scripts/` directory shadows the shipped lanes — the unguarded tofu
    assignment makes a shadowed `delete_tofu` without a map-returning `run` a hard raise here
    (Raises, Tasks).
  Finish by silence: perform no `status`/condition/finalizer/CR mutation here or in the shipped
    tenant delete stages (no `set_status` call exists in any `delete_*.rhai` of this directory) —
    success is the clean return and exit `0`, completion is the controller's finalizer release
    after the `Complete` job, failure is the raise-to-exit(`3`) whose `Failed` job keeps the
    finalizer for a retried run (/operator/src/instance_common.sdd).

Must not:
  Delete from, destroy in or wait inside this file: the per-entry
    `@get_obj` → @delete → @wait_deleted(`60*5` = 300 s) walks of `status.<category>`, the tfstate
    restore + `tf::run_destroy` sequence, and the `*-backups` object sweep all live in the stage
    modules — importing ./../lib/install_from_dir.rhai or ./../lib/wait.rhai here would duplicate
    the lanes' contracts (the delete loops re-walk the recorded lists; there is no `@remove`
    diff-against-applied-set contract on the delete side).
  Gate a rerun skip or a completion on CR state: no read of `status.tag`, conditions or
    finalizers exists here — replays are total and the only skip decisions are the six
    package-directory predicates.

Depends on:
  ./../lib/tofu_gen.rhai — the only import; @has_tofu_files answers the `tofu` gate (its spec
    ./../lib/tofu_gen.sdd).
  The shipped stage modules of this directory, all specs pending: ./delete_posts.rhai,
    ./delete_scalables.rhai, ./delete_others.rhai, ./delete_befores.rhai,
    ./delete_vitals.rhai — each diff-free walks its `instance.status.<category>` entries,
    get-deletes and 300 s-waits them, tolerating NotFound and skiping kinds whose
    @api.exist() is false, and returns the hook-merged context; ./delete_tofu.rhai — restores
    `instance.get_tfstate()` into the tofu dir, regenerates via `tfg::gen_files`, then runs
    the ./../lib/tofu.rhai init+destroy lane; ./delete_backup.rhai — sweeps the
    `*-backups` CronJob/RoleBinding/ConfigMap and label-selected backup/restore Jobs in the
    instance namespace. Six are byte-identical copies of the service twins;
    ./delete_vitals.rhai adds only a commented-out final-backup block. Their internal contracts
    are theirs, quoted here only as lane roles.
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — the three-arg @import_run global shim injected by @Script
    `add_common` (optional-import semantics, skip-vs-rethrow boundary quoted in Raises),
    @is_dir and @type_of.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — the @Script constructor that mounts the above for the agent
    lanes.
  ./context.rhai (+ ./context_tenant.rhai, ./../lib/build_context.rhai) — producer of every
    `context` key; key contracts owned by ./context.sdd, ./context_tenant.sdd and
    ./../lib/build_context.sdd.

References:
  /agent/src/tenant/delete.sdd — the caller: snippet, `instance`/`args` injection, resolver
    directories, its already-gone-CR hard failure (which lands before this module runs), and
    the exit-`3` error lane this script's raises land in.
  ./install.sdd — the tenant install orchestrator: reverses to this lane's bucket order, owns
    the refresh-asymmetry and the install-side unconditional `delete_backup` sweep contrasted
    in Handles, and the shared @import_run hook/merge idiom plus the tofu-lane open points.
  /agent/scripts/service/delete.rhai and /agent/scripts/service/delete.sdd — the diff-verified
    twin; the single-hunk claim in `Purpose` is this file minus the service copy's `crds`
    bucket, matching the role its own spec quotes for tenant.
  /agent/scripts/system/delete.rhai — the different-shape third-kind delete lane.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — why the `crds` bucket is absent: the kind carries no
    CRD-stage surface and its status has no `crds` key.
  /operator/src/instance_common.sdd — the other half of finalization: @do_cleanup releases the
    finalizer only after the delete Job answers `Complete` within the 3-minute wait; a `Failed`
    job re-raises @Error::CleanupJobFailed and the `tenantinstances.vynil.solidite.fr` literal
    (per @InstanceKind::finalizer_name in /operator/src/instancetenant.rs) is held.
  ./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd and ./../lib/wait.sdd — owners of the shared apply/wait
    lanes; the delete stages reuse the @wait_deleted posture without this file touching either.
  /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs and /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs — the service-only
    lifecycle harness and the tenant-dir mock harness that never loads `delete` (Tasks).

Scenario: full bucket order with directories present
  Given a tenant package dir holding all six category directories, a `crds/` directory too, and
    user `.tf` sources, on a live engine with all shipped stage modules resolvable
  When @run executes
  Then the modules are imported in exactly pre → posts → scalables → tofu → (delete_backup →
    vitals) → befores → post order, each guarded bucket merging only a map return and tofu
    assigning its return unguarded — and the `crds/` directory matches no gate anywhere
  And @instance is passed through unchanged — @get_tenant_instance is never called here, so
    every stage reads the pre-script `status` snapshot
  No mapped test: /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs mounts the service dirs only, and
    ./../../tests/fixtures/package holds just `package.yaml` so every gate is false anyway.

Scenario: stock image and empty package skip clean
  Given a stock image (no `delete_pre`/`delete_post` ship) on a package dir with no category
    directories and no user `.tf` file
  When @run executes
  Then both hooks, all five buckets and tofu skip through the @import_run/@is_dir paths with
    debug logs only, and @run returns the hook-skip value error-free
  No mapped test: the service twin's @service_delete_runs_without_error never loads a tenant
    module; a tenant mirror of that posture would at most prove reachability (Tasks).

Scenario: never-installed instance runs lanes without cluster mutation
  Given a package with every category directory present but a CR whose `status` is empty
    (imported, never installed)
  When @run reaches a taken gate and its stage module runs
  Then the stage's set-ness guards over `status` and its `<category>` key short-circuit the
    deletion loop — hooks-only no-op lanes, context returned, nothing deleted, no raise

Scenario: backup sweep rides the vitals directory
  Given a package with a `vitals/` directory and live `*-backups` objects from a scheduled
    backup
  When @run passes the `vitals` gate
  Then `@import_run("delete_backup", ...)` executes BEFORE `delete_vitals` (backup machinery
    goes away before the data stores), and its return — the module's own hook-merged context
    included — is discarded, so `delete_befores` onward never sees backup-lane updates
  But given a package whose `vitals/` directory is absent while backup objects still exist
  Then the sweep lane is skipped entirely even though tenant install sweeps on every run
    (see Tasks)

Scenario: tofu context clobber kills the next gate
  Given a package shadowing `delete_tofu` with a module whose `run` is missing or returns a
    non-map, and a tofu gate that is true
  When @run reaches the tofu exit
  Then `context` becomes `()` (or the non-map) — the assignment carries no @type_of guard —
    and the `${context.package_dir}/others` gate interpolation raises, aborting the delete
    with an error originating between lanes, not inside any stage
  The shipped ./delete_tofu.rhai always returns the context map; no mapped test. Recorded
    behavior, see Tasks.

Scenario: stage throw aborts with no delete-side marker
  Given a bucket stage that fails — a @wait_deleted timeout, a `tf::run_destroy` raise from
    ./delete_tofu.rhai, or any non-skip error re-thrown by a stage
  When the throw crosses @import_run
  Then it is not one of the two skip markers, so it re-throws: no later bucket, no backup
    sweep, no `delete_post`, and no `set_status_*` failure write exists anywhere on the tenant
    delete lane to record it — the Rust lane logs its exit-`3` text and the controller sees a
    `Failed` job, holds the finalizer and retries the delete
  No mapped test.

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the Scenarios to a tenant delete suite: no test runs this file today —
      /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs is service-only and
      /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs shows the tenant mock harness works but loads only the
      backup-prepare/restore modules. Add a fixture package with category dirs and mock stage
      modules pinning the nine-call order, the gate predicates, the merge posture and the
      throw-abort on the mock engine.
  [ ] Author the seven pending stage specs listed under `Depends on`; their quoted lane roles
      here (get-delete-wait walk, 300 s waits, tfstate restore, backup sweep) must be verified
      there, not restated.
  [?] Backup sweep gated by the `vitals` DIRECTORY: a package that scheduled backups and later
      shipped without `vitals/` (or whose update removed the dir) never runs `delete_backup` on
      delete — the backup CronJob/Jobs/RoleBinding/ConfigMap outlive the instance while install
      sweeps on every run. Decide whether the delete-side sweep gate should key on
      `instance.status.vitals` or the `backup-settings` Secret instead.
  [?] Bucket skipping is directory-based, status-blind: `status.<category>` entries whose
      directory is absent at delete time are never deleted, yet the run returns clean and the
      controller releases the finalizer — recorded resources orphan silently. Decide whether a
      non-empty status bucket must force its lane regardless of the directory.
  [?] Unguarded tofu return (Scenario "tofu context clobber"): a package-shaped
      `delete_tofu` turns the whole delete into a property-on-`()` raise at the `others` gate
      with a misleading error origin. ./install.sdd holds the adjacent open point (its stale
      `ctx` re-merge); decide one guarded pattern for both twins and lanes.
  [?] `delete_post` return is discarded while `delete_pre` merges — nothing runs after the post
      hook, so a merge today feeds no consumer; install merges its twin for symmetry. Decide
      whether the asymmetry (or install's merge) should change.
  [?] The final-backup-before-teardown intent survives only as the two TODO comments in
      ./delete_vitals.rhai — the tenant copy additionally ships a commented-out manual-backup
      block (rendering `manualbackup.yaml` over `context.tenant.namespaces`) that the service
      twin lacks; the current sequence sweeps backup machinery and then deletes the data stores
      with no last backup taken. Decide when ./delete_vitals.sdd is authored whether delete
      triggers and waits a final backup first, and whether the dead block stays.
  [?] Twin-drift watch: this orchestrator and six of its seven stage modules are byte-identical
      copies of the service files (this file differing by the one `crds` hunk,
      ./delete_vitals.rhai by the comment block), so a service-side fix must be hand-copied
      here. Decide whether the orchestrator body should be factored into a shared lib module
      with a kind hook.

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a passing mapped test or a recorded decision, the nine-call order and
    gate texts above still match the source, the seven stage specs exist, and `specdd lint` is
    green on this file.
